mdio-rtl-otto: tolerate a switch port whose PHY is on a foreign MDIO bus

The driver assumes every switch-port phy-handle resolves to a PHY on one of
its own buses, and fails the whole probe otherwise.  On the CR1000A the MoCA
port's MXL3711 hangs off the SoC's MDIO controller instead, whose "reg" is a
register address rather than a bus index, so probe died with
"mdio@90000 illegal bus number" and none of the switch's real port PHYs -
lan1, lan2, lan10g - ever came up.

Skip such a port instead: it is not this controller's to drive, and phylink
connects it through the foreign bus on its own.

--- a/mdio-realtek-otto.c
+++ b/mdio-realtek-otto.c
@@ -1034,8 +1034,18 @@
 			return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL, "%pfwP no bus number\n",
 					     fw_bus ?: fw_phy);
 
-		if (smi_bus >= ctrl->cfg->num_buses)
-			return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL, "%pfwP illegal bus number\n", fw_bus);
+		/* A switch port's PHY does not have to sit on THIS controller's
+		 * buses: the CR1000A reaches its MoCA PHY over the SoC's own
+		 * MDIO bus.  Such a port is not ours to drive - leave it to
+		 * phylink and carry on instead of failing the whole probe with
+		 * "illegal bus number" (the foreign controller's reg is an
+		 * address, not a bus index).
+		 */
+		if (smi_bus >= ctrl->cfg->num_buses) {
+			dev_dbg(dev, "%pfwP: PHY on a foreign MDIO bus, skipping\n",
+				fw_port);
+			continue;
+		}
 
 		if (fwnode_device_is_compatible(fw_phy, "ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c45"))
 			ctrl->bus[smi_bus].is_c45 = true;
